.TH COMUNICADO 1 "August 2025" "comunicado 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
comunicado \- Modern TUI-based email and calendar client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B comunicado
[\fIOPTION\fR]... [\fICOMMAND\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Comunicado is a modern terminal-based email and calendar client built for
terminal power users, privacy-conscious developers, and system administrators.

It provides native HTML email rendering, OAuth2 authentication, CalDAV calendar
integration, and a plugin architecture, all within a modern terminal user
interface.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-config\-dir\fR \fIDIR\fR
Use custom configuration directory
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enable verbose logging
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress non-essential output
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Show help information
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Show version information

.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBsetup\fR
Run the interactive setup wizard to configure email accounts and calendar
.TP
\fBconfig\fR
Manage configuration settings
.TP
\fBnotes\fR
Manage notes using the Notes plugin
.TP
\fBkde\-connect\fR
Interact with KDE Connect devices

.SH FEATURES
.IP \[bu] 2
Modern TUI interface with ratatui framework
.IP \[bu] 2
HTML email rendering with images and animations
.IP \[bu] 2
OAuth2 support for Gmail, Outlook, and other providers
.IP \[bu] 2
CalDAV calendar integration with bidirectional sync
.IP \[bu] 2
Plugin architecture with Notes and KDE Connect plugins
.IP \[bu] 2
Maildir support for local email storage
.IP \[bu] 2
Advanced search and email threading
.IP \[bu] 2
Desktop notifications and customizable keyboard shortcuts

.SH FILES
.TP
\fB~/.config/comunicado/config.toml\fR
Main configuration file
.TP
\fB~/.local/share/comunicado/\fR
Local data directory for emails and calendar
.TP
\fB~/.cache/comunicado/\fR
Cache directory for images and temporary data

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
\fBcomunicado\fR
Start the main TUI interface
.TP
\fBcomunicado setup\fR
Run the setup wizard for first-time configuration
.TP
\fBcomunicado notes create "Meeting Notes"\fR
Create a new note using the Notes plugin
.TP
\fBcomunicado kde-connect devices\fR
List available KDE Connect devices

.SH SUPPORTED TERMINALS
Comunicado works best with modern terminals that support graphics protocols:
.IP \[bu] 2
Kitty (recommended for full graphics support)
.IP \[bu] 2
Foot (Wayland native with good performance)
.IP \[bu] 2
WezTerm (cross-platform with advanced features)
.IP \[bu] 2
Most xterm-compatible terminals (limited graphics)

